ok then review gmail for these reports Continued through **B05 and B06**, and both full runs were emailed with Markdown + JSON attachments.

B05 confirmed the process should score **lifecycle/problem cells**, not whole sectors. Ireland has 498,283 registered domestic wastewater systems, but routine emptying and standard servicing are already partly commoditized. The stronger cell is **failed inspection → Advisory Notice → grant route → site-specific remediation → comparable compliant quotes**. The top seven counties contain 50.62% of registered systems, and grant awards rose from 194 in 2023 to 460 in 2025 after the grant redesign. ([Central Statistics Office][1])

B06 produced an even stronger structural insight. UK home EV charging has an estimated **~1.4 million installed home chargers**, while official grant schemes have funded 412,682 domestic installations since 2013. Zappi, Ohme and Hypervolt commonly have **3-year standard warranties**. Myenergi explicitly requires faults to go through its own assessment/approved warranty installer and warns unauthorized repairs can void warranty. ([Zapmap][2])

Yet once that protection expires, independent economics change sharply. A Zappi PCB repair is currently advertised at **£169**, while comparable replacement installations are roughly **£999–£1,100+**. In the selected price comparison, qualifying PCB repair is about **16% of installed replacement cost**. Independent specialists also advertise multi-brand and national mail-in PCB repair. ([WSMFix][3])

That gives GoldProbe a major refinement:

> **Channel openness is not a market-level constant. It changes with warranty status, asset age, model and fault type.**

The canonical grain should increasingly be:

`country × asset × model × install cohort × warranty status × lifecycle stage × fault × geography`

rather than:

`country × sector → score`.

B06 generated three mechanism candidates worth testing independently: **`WARRANTY_EXPIRY_CHANNEL_FLIP`** — assets move from OEM-controlled to independent repair channels after warranty; **`REMOVABLE_CONTROL_BOARD_DELOCALIZES_REPAIR`** — removable electronics turn an inherently local installed asset into a national parcel-logistics repair market; and **`INSTALLATION_WAVE_LAGGED_AFTERMARKET`** — installation booms potentially create predictable repair waves several years later.

